# WHAT IS NOT PINNED, AND WHY.
#
# Upstream v0.7.0 carries three folders under its docs/ that this file has never
# named, and after reading them the answer is still no:
#
#   docs/decisions/  — upstream's own ADRs and CRDs (19 files at this tag);
#   docs/design/     — upstream's own task breakdown (1 file);
#   docs/qa/         — upstream's QA cases, its run-all.sh and its qa lib (75).
#
# Ninety-five files, and every one of them is upstream's record of upstream's own
# jobs. None of them holds a rule this port carries, skips or restates, which is
# the test ADR 0005 set for a pinned line. Pinning them would report dozens of
# FAILED lines per pass that say nothing about this port, and a check nobody reads
# is worse than no check, because it looks like one.
#
# The same goes for package.json, tools/, preset/, .github/workflows/ and
# cordis.patch.yml: nothing there is ported, and porting.md's "did not port"
# table names each of them with its reason.
#
# One thing to know anyway: upstream's docs/decisions/ holds the reasoning behind
# some of the nine divergences above — its own CRD 0009 is what entry 7 argues
# with. When a divergence row is in question, read those from the clone by hand.
# That is a person's job, not a checksum's.
